  "limitations": [
    "Old and current workloads/toolchain binaries differ despite identical pinned model/source/loading settings. Below85 success is not universal proof for current full tasks.",
    "Observed percentage is kernel memorystatus level, not literal raw free-page bytes or an application/GPU budget.",
    "Mei is present in process telemetry; its roughly1.4GiB OS footprint does not cover the roughly19.46GiB MLX allocator peak. Do not use process sum as total model memory.",
    "Older lower-headroom failures used other runtime revisions or loader/prefill profiles and must not be treated as matched threshold tests."
  ],
  "finding": "Blanket85 launch cutoff was precautionary, not a calibrated minimum; existing successful81/82 runs contradict universal necessity. A single launch percentage also cannot prevent later external workload pressure.",
